<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>The economic issues and policy in France - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 05:36:18 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>Southwest France steps up mosquito control following 20 chikungunya cases</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260819-southwest-france-steps-up-mosquito-control-following-20-chikungunya-cases</link><description>
Mosquito control operations are being stepped up across southwestern France after more than 20 locally contracted cases of the chikungunya virus were recorded since the beginning of August, with infections reported in three departments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/814394b8-9b0a-11f1-9920-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP06022202255.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/814394b8-9b0a-11f1-9920-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP06022202255.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">de6ad742-9b09-11f1-87cd-c39a7a52be8b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 05:16:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/814394b8-9b0a-11f1-9920-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP06022202255.jpg">© Adrien/AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Warnings sent to French taxpayers after hackers allegedly sell stolen data</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260818-french-taxpayers-receive-warnings-after-hackers-steal-and-allegedly-sell-data</link><description>
More than 670,000 French taxpayers are being notified that their personal and tax information has been stolen in cyber attacks on the French tax office and allegedly sold online.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71b9a2a0-13c9-11ea-9449-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/impots.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71b9a2a0-13c9-11ea-9449-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/impots.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11dab6b2-9aea-11f1-a568-eb68b4f1f89b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:37:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71b9a2a0-13c9-11ea-9449-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/impots.jpg">AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Iran bars two French diplomats over alleged 'interference'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260817-iran-bars-two-french-diplomats-over-alleged-interference</link><description>
Iran has said ​that two French embassy employees who were briefly detained last month following a ​diplomatic dispute will not be allowed to return to Iran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3a30ab80-89b0-11f1-afab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96TM9DK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3a30ab80-89b0-11f1-afab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96TM9DK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7580d2a-9a2a-11f1-97ca-c954d7c983a2</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:33:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3a30ab80-89b0-11f1-afab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96TM9DK.jpg">© AFP - Atta Kenare</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French PM Lecornu says aid available 'immediately' to rebuild fire-hit regions</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260817-french-pm-lecornu-says-aid-available-immediately-to-rebuild-fire-hit-regions</link><description>
French Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu on Monday announced aid worth €12 million to help residents of the southwest hit by wildfires rebuild their lives. He was heckled earlier in the day by dozens of locals in the town of Le Porge in the Gironde region, who said they were unhappy with the government's response.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fe13c2a8-8dd4-11f1-a326-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fe13c2a8-8dd4-11f1-a326-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b92d9c8-9a5e-11f1-aa90-15d3b6b8ca68</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:23:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fe13c2a8-8dd4-11f1-a326-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NU.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Devastated by wildfire, the village of Le Porge pins hopes for support on PM visit</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260817-devastated-by-wildfire-the-village-of-le-porge-pins-hopes-for-support-on-pm-visit</link><description>
Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu will visit the Gironde department in southwestern France on Monday to launch reconstruction efforts, after the area fell victim to the most destructive wildfires seen in 70 years. The mayor of Le Porge – one of the villages worst affected – told RFI he's hoping for government support to rebuild its economy, which relies heavily on forest exploitation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69b874be-9662-11f1-82a8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/260810-Le-Porge-burnt-traffic-sign3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69b874be-9662-11f1-82a8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/260810-Le-Porge-burnt-traffic-sign3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">006ea6ee-9636-11f1-af94-35fc75775395</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 05:13:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69b874be-9662-11f1-82a8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/260810-Le-Porge-burnt-traffic-sign3.jpg">© RFI/Jan van der Made</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Obesity rises sharply as French Polynesia faces chronic health challenges</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260816-obesity-rises-sharply-as-french-polynesia-faces-chronic-health-challenges</link><description>
French Polynesia is facing growing public health pressures as rising rates of chronic disease combine with an ageing population and changing lifestyles. More than half of adult residents are now considered obese.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6609f082-9571-11f1-8997-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/French-Polynesia-Obesity.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6609f082-9571-11f1-8997-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/French-Polynesia-Obesity.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">142ad854-9570-11f1-80d1-6bca3bd6865c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:31:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6609f082-9571-11f1-8997-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/French-Polynesia-Obesity.jpg">© AFP - THEO ROUBY </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ex-PM Attal urges Macron to put under-15 social media ban to referendum</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260816-ex-pm-attal-urges-macron-to-put-under-15-social-media-ban-to-referendum</link><description>
Gabriel Attal has called on President Emmanuel Macron to put a proposed ban on social media for children under 15 directly to French voters, after the Constitutional Council struck down legislation approved by parliament.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8acb7a0-1e30-11f1-8f66-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24066822349898.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8acb7a0-1e30-11f1-8f66-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24066822349898.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6f3b6e46-9955-11f1-adb7-9f8fc4277402</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:30:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8acb7a0-1e30-11f1-8f66-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24066822349898.jpg">AP - Jenny Kane</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France probes unprecedented cyberattack after tax data of 678,000 users stolen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260815-france-probes-unprecedented-cyberattack-after-tax-data-of-678-000-users-stolen</link><description>
French prosecutors have opened an investigation into a major cyberattack on the country’s tax administration that affected nearly 700,000 individuals and businesses, authorities said on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ef8055a-98b7-11f1-8465-5f55dfe1c00c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:50:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg">© Freepix</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's successive heatwaves show strain of living in urban 'heat islands'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260815-france-s-successive-heatwaves-highlight-strain-of-living-in-urban-heat-islands</link><description>
As France experiences its latest heatwave, residents of urban "heat islands" – dense neighbourhoods with few trees or green spaces – are suffering acutely in the high temperatures, and local authorities are searching for solutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e08ea958-97db-11f1-ac97-c132d391fb73</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:43:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg">© Théo Renaudon/RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Law on assisted dying wins constitutional approval in France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-law-on-assisted-dying-wins-constitutional-approval-in-france</link><description>
France's Constitutional Council on Friday approved a law creating a right to assisted dying, removing the last major legal obstacle before the measure can be enacted and implemented.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26163be6-97ee-11f1-94eb-8707596c334a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:11:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg">© AFP - JEAN-CHRISTOPHE VERHAEGEN </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Top French court scraps social media ban for children under 15</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-top-french-court-scraps-social-media-ban-for-children-under-15</link><description>
France's Constitutional Council struck down a law on Friday that would have banned children under 15 from using social media from September. The judges ruled that the measure placed a disproportionate restriction on freedom of expression and communication.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/21dd94ca-97e4-11f1-8302-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25149163043530.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/21dd94ca-97e4-11f1-8302-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25149163043530.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66562b0e-97e3-11f1-9c2d-3774d7b74ff3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:59:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/21dd94ca-97e4-11f1-8302-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25149163043530.jpg">© AP - Kiichiro Sato </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French firefighters threaten to strike over lack of resources</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-french-firefighters-threaten-to-strike-over-lack-of-resources</link><description>
As wildfires continue to burn across France, representatives of firefighters' unions said they would go on strike in September to protest a lack of resources. Despite a meeting with the interior minister on Thursday, they say they are unhappy with the government's response so far.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ed94ca0-8b72-11f1-8c21-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209755840474.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ed94ca0-8b72-11f1-8c21-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209755840474.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3c773d2-97bc-11f1-ac7a-91dcbd8159e7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:39:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ed94ca0-8b72-11f1-8c21-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209755840474.jpg">© AP Photo/Emma Da Silva</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France gripped by latest summer heatwave as drought conditions worsen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260812-france-gripped-by-latest-summer-heatwave-as-drought-conditions-worsen</link><description>
Scorching heat continued to spread across most of mainland France on Wednesday, as the Ministry for Ecological Transition met to take stock of the effects of a drought that has been steadily worsening since May. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee532400-9624-11f1-9288-8fc7ca80b067</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:38:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg">REUTERS - Stephane Mahe</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Assisted dying, social media and agriculture put France’s top court in spotlight</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260811-assisted-dying-social-media-and-agriculture-put-france-s-top-court-in-spotlight</link><description>
France’s Constitutional Council is facing a politically charged end to the summer, with judges due to rule on a series of high-profile laws – including those covering assisted dying, social media use by children, agriculture and public security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">794857bc-956f-11f1-8018-6bca3bd6865c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:01:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg">© Christophe BONNET</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France introduces tough fines for unsolicited telemarketing calls</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260811-france-introduces-tough-fines-for-unsolicited-telemarketing-calls</link><description>
France has banned unsolicited telemarketing calls under a new law to protect consumers and shield vulnerable people from fraudulent commercial practices. Individuals who make illegal calls can be fined up to €75,000 per call when the new law comes into effect on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0696e0c0-93f4-11f1-b693-771bd1b13781</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 05:56:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg">© Michael Sohn / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>May ’68 protest leader Cohn-Bendit pledges support to Glucksmann for 2027</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260810-may-68-veteran-cohn-bendit-throws-support-behind-left-wing-glucksmann-for-2027</link><description>
Former Green MEP Daniel Cohn-Bendit, a historic figure on the French left, on Monday gave his support to Raphaël Glucksmann for France’s 2027 presidential election, in an interview with Le Point magazine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a90b0ffe-94b5-11f1-ba5c-c57808d5257e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:00:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg">AFP - LOU BENOIST</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Extreme heat exposes crisis inside Europe's overcrowded prisons</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260810-extreme-heat-exposes-crisis-inside-europe-s-overcrowded-prisons</link><description>
Record summer temperatures are exposing the strain on overcrowded prisons across France, Italy and Belgium, where ageing buildings and poor ventilation are making extreme heat increasingly difficult to manage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eef4dfb4-7ba5-11f1-a224-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-78T66KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eef4dfb4-7ba5-11f1-a224-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-78T66KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">afed2446-925e-11f1-99f0-15ecfd29aa41</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 04:37:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eef4dfb4-7ba5-11f1-a224-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-78T66KE.jpg">AFP - JEAN-FRANCOIS MONIER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Rise in injuries sees Paris police impose new rules on e-scooter users</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260809-rise-in-injuries-sees-paris-council-impose-new-rules-on-e-scooter-users</link><description>
Electric scooter riders in Paris must now wear helmets and reflective gear under new rules introduced after a significant rise in injuries involving the two-wheelers, police said at the weekend. 
